 seat Safe or Solid Republican", "Teixeira holds a huge money edge ($3.9M vs $244k raised, plus ~$930k outside support) and Trump's endorsement", "Open R+10 seat with no public general-election polls, keeping uncertainty elevated", "Democratic-leaning national environment is the main force narrowing an open seat"], "rationale": "Every expert rater puts this open, ten-points-Republican district firmly in the GOP column, markets price the Democrat at about six percent, and Teixeira's roughly sixteen-to-one fundraising advantage leaves Hook little visible path; only the favorable national environment for Democrats keeps this short of Safe Republican.", "watch": "With no public polling, an independent survey showing Hook within single digits, or a further national shift toward Democrats, would be the clearest sign this open seat is becoming competitive.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Chip Roy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's 21st District is an open Republican-held seat running from Austin's western suburbs toward San Antonio's northern reaches, with a partisan lean of about ten points toward the GOP. Chip Roy's retirement to run for state attorney general leaves the seat open, and Republicans nominated former MLB star Mark Teixeira, who won President Trump's endorsement in February. Democrat Kristin Hook, a scientist, took her party's nomination in March.\n\nThe evidence points firmly Republican. All nine expert raters call the seat Safe or Solid R, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at roughly six percent. Teixeira has raised about $3.9 million to Hook's $244,000 and benefits from more than $900,000 in outside support. With no public general-election polling, uncertainty runs somewhat higher than usual, but the Democratic-tilted national environment is the main thing that could narrow what is otherwise a clear Republican advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0352, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0372, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0688, "margin": -11.5}]}